['spain-fabada','Fabada Asturiana (Asturian White Bean and Sausage Stew)','Spain','🇪🇸',165,['white beans','chorizo','black pudding','pork shoulder','pork belly','saffron','water'],[[110,'g'],[45,'g'],[40,'g'],[55,'g'],[30,'g'],[4,'strand'],[550,'ml']],'https://www.spain.info/en/recipe/fabada/',['Soak the beans overnight, drain, and place them in a wide pot with fresh water.','Add pork shoulder and pork belly, bring slowly to a simmer, and skim the surface.','Cook gently until the beans are nearly tender, then add chorizo, black pudding, and saffron.','Simmer until creamy and safely cooked, rest for fifteen minutes, and serve the sliced meats alongside.']],
['spain-pulpo-feira','Pulpo a Feira (Galician Paprika Octopus)','Spain','🇪🇸',55,['octopus','onion','olive oil','sweet paprika','hot paprika','coarse salt','water'],[[260,'g'],[50,'g'],[1.5,'tbsp'],[0.5,'tsp'],[0.125,'tsp'],[2,'g'],[700,'ml']],'https://www.spain.info/en/recipe/pulpo-feira/',['Bring the water and onion to a boil and dip the cleaned octopus in and out three times.','Lower the octopus into the pot and simmer until tender but the skin remains intact.','Drain, rest briefly, and cut the tentacles into bite-size rounds.','Arrange warm, season with coarse salt and both paprikas, and drizzle with olive oil.']],
['spain-marmitako','Marmitako (Basque Tuna and Potato Stew)','Spain','🇪🇸',40,['tuna','potato','red bell pepper','green bell pepper','tomato','onion','fish stock'],[[170,'g'],[220,'g'],[70,'g'],[60,'g'],[120,'g'],[70,'g'],[350,'ml']],'https://www.spain.info/es/receta/marmitako/',['Soften onion and both peppers in a spoonful of olive oil, then add chopped tomato.','Add broken potato chunks and hot fish stock and simmer until the potato is almost tender.','Cut tuna into large cubes and place them over the stew.','Cover and cook gently just until the tuna is opaque and safely cooked, then rest for five minutes.']],
['spain-salmorejo','Salmorejo Cordobés (Andalusian Thick Tomato and Bread Soup)','Spain','🇪🇸',20,['tomato','rustic bread','olive oil','garlic','egg','serrano ham','salt'],[[300,'g'],[60,'g'],[1.5,'tbsp'],[0.5,'clove'],[0.5,'piece'],[25,'g'],[1,'g']],'https://www.spain.info/es/receta/salmorejo/',['Blend the ripe tomato until smooth and strain out seeds and coarse skin.','Soak the bread in the tomato for five minutes, then add garlic and salt.','Blend while slowly adding olive oil until thick, pale, and emulsified; chill.','Top with chopped boiled egg and serrano ham immediately before serving.']],
['spain-fideua','Fideuà Valenciana (Valencian Seafood Noodle Paella)','Spain','🇪🇸',45,['short noodles','shrimp','monkfish','cuttlefish','tomato','fish stock','saffron'],[[100,'g'],[90,'g'],[90,'g'],[70,'g'],[60,'g'],[330,'ml'],[4,'strand']],'https://www.spain.info/es/receta/fideua/',['Sear shrimp briefly in olive oil and reserve; brown the monkfish and cuttlefish in the same pan.','Add grated tomato and cook until concentrated, then stir in the noodles.','Pour in hot fish stock with saffron and simmer without excessive stirring.','Return the shrimp and cook until the noodles absorb the stock and all seafood is safely cooked.']],
['spain-escalivada','Escalivada Catalana (Catalan Roasted Pepper and Eggplant)','Spain','🇪🇸',50,['eggplant','red bell pepper','garlic','olive oil','sherry vinegar','salt'],[[180,'g'],[180,'g'],[1,'clove'],[1.5,'tbsp'],[1,'tsp'],[1,'g']],'https://www.spain.info/es/receta/escalivada/',['Roast the whole eggplant and pepper at 220°C until collapsed and charred in places.','Cover for ten minutes, then peel the vegetables and remove the pepper seeds.','Tear the flesh into long strips and arrange it with finely chopped garlic.','Season with salt, vinegar, and olive oil and rest before serving warm or at room temperature.']],
['spain-cocido-madrileno','Cocido Madrileño (Madrid Chickpea, Meat, and Vegetable Stew)','Spain','🇪🇸',210,['chickpeas','beef shank','chicken thigh','chorizo','potato','cabbage','carrot','fine noodles'],[[90,'g'],[100,'g'],[100,'g'],[35,'g'],[140,'g'],[120,'g'],[70,'g'],[35,'g']],'https://www.spain.info/es/receta/cocido-madrileno/',['Soak the chickpeas overnight; simmer beef and chicken in 800 ml water, skimming well.','Add chickpeas and carrot and cook gently until the meat and chickpeas approach tenderness.','Cook chorizo separately; add potato near the end and boil cabbage in a second pan.','Cook noodles in strained broth and serve in three parts: soup, chickpeas with vegetables, then sliced meats.']],
['spain-migas-extremenas','Migas Extremeñas (Extremaduran Fried Bread Crumbs with Pork)','Spain','🇪🇸',35,['stale bread','pork belly','garlic','dried red pepper','sweet paprika','olive oil','water'],[[140,'g'],[70,'g'],[2,'clove'],[1,'piece'],[0.5,'tsp'],[1,'tbsp'],[45,'ml']],'https://www.spain.info/es/receta/migas-extremenas/',['Break the stale bread into small crumbs, sprinkle evenly with water, and rest covered.','Fry garlic and dried pepper in olive oil, remove them, then crisp the pork belly.','Lower the heat, add paprika and the damp bread crumbs, and stir continuously.','Cook until the crumbs are loose and golden, then return the garlic, pepper, and pork.']],
['spain-arroz-negro','Arroz Negro (Balearic Squid-Ink Rice)','Spain','🇪🇸',40,['rice','baby squid','fish stock','tomato','onion','garlic','sweet paprika'],[[95,'g'],[170,'g'],[300,'ml'],[90,'g'],[50,'g'],[1,'clove'],[0.5,'tsp']],'https://www.spain.info/es/receta/arroz-negro/',['Soften onion in olive oil, add squid, and cook until it begins to colour.','Stir in garlic, grated tomato, paprika, and the squid ink released during cleaning.','Add rice, coat it in the mixture, and pour in hot fish stock.','Cook briskly for five minutes, then gently until the rice is tender and the seafood safely cooked.']],
['spain-crema-catalana','Crema Catalana (Catalan Lemon Custard with Caramel Crust)','Spain','🇪🇸',35,['milk','egg yolk','sugar','cornstarch','lemon','cinnamon stick'],[[250,'ml'],[2,'piece'],[45,'g'],[12,'g'],[0.25,'piece'],[0.5,'piece']],'https://www.spain.info/en/recipe/crema-catalana/',['Warm most of the milk with lemon peel and cinnamon, then remove from heat to infuse.','Whisk egg yolks, 30 g sugar, cornstarch, and the reserved cold milk until smooth.','Strain in the warm milk and stir over low heat until the custard coats a spoon.','Chill in a shallow dish, scatter with remaining sugar, and caramelize the surface just before serving.']]
